---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About | ALMA AI">

<section class="about">

    <div class="about-container">

        <div class="card">

            <span class="badge">
                About
            </span>

            <h1>
                Understanding is harder than information.
            </h1>

            <p class="intro">

                We live in a world where information is nearly free.

                Answers arrive instantly.

                Advice is everywhere.

                Ask an AI almost anything, and it will explain it to you in seconds.

            </p>

            <p>

                And yet — people still don't understand themselves.

                Or each other.

            </p>

            <p>

                That contradiction is where ALMA began.

            </p>

            <h2>
                Why This Project Exists
            </h2>

            <p>

                ALMA didn't start as an AI product.

                It started with years of watching the same pattern repeat — in relationships, in difficult decisions, in conversations that circled the same unresolved thing without ever naming it.

            </p>

            <p>

                The people involved weren't confused.

                They weren't lacking information.

                Most of them could explain their situation clearly, analyze it, even give good advice to someone else in the same position.

            </p>

            <p>

                They just couldn't see it clearly from the inside.

            </p>

            <div class="quote">

                Information was never the problem.

                <br>

                <strong>Understanding was.</strong>

            </div>

            <h2>
                More Than Conversation
            </h2>

            <p>

                Large language models made talking to AI feel natural.

                That changed everything about what people expect from these systems.

            </p>

            <p>

                But talking isn't understanding.

            </p>

            <p>

                Understanding — between two people, or between a person and an AI — takes continuity.

                It requires memory that means something, not just memory that stores something.

                It requires being willing to revise what you thought you knew, instead of generating a fresh, confident answer every single time.

            </p>

            <p>

                That's the direction ALMA is exploring.

            </p>

            <h2>
                Our Principles
            </h2>

            <p>

                A few things we believe should stay true no matter how far AI advances.

            </p>

            <p>

                <strong>People are more than labels.</strong>

                No personality type, diagnosis, or category fully describes a human being — and a system that pretends otherwise isn't understanding you, it's filing you.

            </p>

            <p>

                <strong>Understanding should stay uncertain.</strong>

                Good reasoning holds uncertainty instead of faking confidence it hasn't earned.

            </p>

            <p>

                <strong>Memory should sharpen judgment, not just recall facts.</strong>

                Remembering what someone said is easy.

                Remembering what it meant — and how that meaning shifted over time — is the hard part, and the only part that matters.

            </p>

            <p>

                <strong>AI should show its work.</strong>

                If a system reaches a conclusion about you, you should be able to see why.

                Understanding you shouldn't come with a black box attached.

            </p>

            <h2>
                Looking Forward
            </h2>

            <p>

                Relationships are only the starting point.

            </p>

            <p>

                If AI can genuinely learn to understand long-term human compatibility, the applications reach much further: partners whose values actually align, friendships that last, teams that keep working well together for years, researchers who collaborate without friction.

            </p>

            <p>

                There's a useful precedent already.

                Astronauts aren't selected for long-duration missions on technical skill alone — psychological compatibility is treated as just as critical, because a crew sealed together for months can't survive on competence alone.

            </p>

            <p>

                We think that principle generalizes.

                Compatibility, understood well, may become one of the most valuable things AI can help people see clearly — not by deciding for them, but by making what's already true about a relationship visible sooner.

            </p>

            <h2>
                A Different Direction
            </h2>

            <p>

                ALMA isn't trying to be a better chatbot.

            </p>

            <p>

                We're trying to find out if AI can become something else entirely: a system that remembers responsibly, reasons transparently, and actually gets to know the person it's working with — not just the last thing they typed.

            </p>

            <p>

                We don't know yet if that's fully possible.

            </p>

            <div class="quote">

                That uncertainty isn't a weakness in the pitch.

                <br>

                <strong>It's the reason the project exists at all.</strong>

            </div>

            <h2>
                About the Founder
            </h2>

            <div class="founder">

                <img
                    src="/images/founder-maksim-nagaev.jpg"
                    alt="Maksim Nagaev, founder of ALMA"
                    class="founder-photo"
                />

                <div class="founder-text">

                    <p class="founder-name">
                        Maksim Nagaev
                    </p>

                    <p>

                        ALMA is an independent research initiative created by Maksim Nagaev.

                    </p>

                    <p>

                        The project began with a simple observation: people often understand complex ideas more easily than they understand themselves.

                        They can explain relationships, spot patterns in other people's lives, and give thoughtful advice — yet struggle to see the same patterns when it's their own life in question.

                    </p>

                    <p>

                        That observation slowly turned into a bigger question: could AI become more than a conversational tool?

                        Could it become something that helps a person build a deeper understanding of themselves over time?

                    </p>

                    <p>

                        ALMA exists to find out.

                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>

</Layout>

<style>

@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,340..600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap');

.about{

    padding:100px 24px 140px;
    background:#f8fafc;
    font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;

}

.about-container{

    max-width:900px;
    margin:0 auto;

}

.card{

    max-width:740px;
    margin:0 auto;

}

.badge{

    display:inline-block;
    padding:8px 18px;
    border-radius:999px;
    background:#eef4ff;
    color:#2563eb;
    font-size:13px;
    font-weight:600;
    letter-spacing:.06em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    margin-bottom:26px;

}

.card h1{

    font-family:'Fraunces',serif;
    font-optical-sizing:auto;
    font-weight:440;
    font-size:46px;
    line-height:1.22;
    letter-spacing:-.01em;
    color:#111827;
    margin:0 0 40px;

}

.card h2{

    font-family:'Fraunces',serif;
    font-weight:460;
    font-size:28px;
    line-height:1.3;
    color:#111827;
    margin:64px 0 22px;

}

.card p{

    font-size:18px;
    line-height:1.85;
    color:#3f495a;
    margin:0 0 22px;

}

.card .intro{

    font-size:20px;
    line-height:1.75;
    color:#111827;

}

.card p strong{

    color:#111827;
    font-weight:650;

}

.quote{

    position:relative;

    margin:48px 0;
    padding:8px 0 8px 28px;

    border-left:3px solid #2563eb;

    font-family:'Fraunces',serif;
    font-weight:420;
    font-style:italic;
    font-size:25px;
    line-height:1.5;
    letter-spacing:-.005em;
    color:#1e293b;

}

.quote strong{

    font-style:normal;
    font-weight:600;
    color:#111827;

}

.founder{

    display:flex;
    gap:36px;
    align-items:flex-start;

    margin-top:8px;
    padding:40px;

    background:#ffffff;
    border:1px solid #e3e8ef;
    border-radius:24px;

}

.founder-photo{

    flex-shrink:0;

    width:132px;
    height:132px;

    border-radius:999px;

    object-fit:cover;

    box-shadow:0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.10);

}

.founder-text{

    flex:1;
    min-width:0;

}

.founder-name{

    font-family:'Fraunces',serif;
    font-weight:520;
    font-size:20px;
    color:#111827;
    margin:0 0 14px !important;

}

.founder-text p{

    font-size:16px;
    line-height:1.75;

}

.founder-text p:last-child{

    margin-bottom:0;

}

@media(max-width:760px){

    .about{

        padding:64px 20px 100px;

    }

    .card h1{

        font-size:32px;
        margin-bottom:28px;

    }

    .card h2{

        font-size:23px;
        margin:48px 0 18px;

    }

    .card p{

        font-size:16px;

    }

    .card .intro{

        font-size:18px;

    }

    .quote{

        font-size:20px;
        padding-left:20px;
        margin:36px 0;

    }

    .founder{

        flex-direction:column;
        align-items:center;
        text-align:center;
        padding:32px 24px;
        gap:24px;

    }

    .founder-photo{

        width:112px;
        height:112px;

    }

}

</style>
